<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Israel</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as State of Israel</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Israel is a country in the Southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/levant">Levant</a> region of West <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia">Asia</a>, on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a> coast, bordered by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lebanon">Lebanon</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a>, Jordan and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zionism">Zionism</a>, which sought a homeland for the Jewish people in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palestine">Palestine</a>, grew from European antisemitism in the late 19th century. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> established Mandatory Palestine in 1920, and in 1947 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-nations">United Nations</a> proposed partitioning the land between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jews">Jews</a> and the Arab-majority population. Israel declared independence on 14 May 1948, and neighbouring Arab states invaded the next day. Most Palestinian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabs">Arabs</a> fled or were expelled during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nakba">Nakba</a>, and the Israeli–Palestinian conflict persists.</p></div>
